# AI Engineering Operating System

For material engineering work, use the `ai-engineering-operating-system` skill from `.agents/skills/ai-engineering-os/`.

## Operating Rules

- Classify the request FAST, STANDARD, or ENTERPRISE before selecting process depth.
- Ground implementation plans in repository evidence. Distinguish facts from inference.
- For STANDARD and ENTERPRISE work, keep durable artifacts under `.ai-engineering/` unless the repository already has authoritative equivalents.
- Plan first when the task is ambiguous, cross-cutting, or high-risk.
- Use independent review: the same implementation context must not be the sole reviewer for STANDARD or ENTERPRISE work. Use a separate Codex thread/agent/worktree or a human reviewer.
- Parallelize only tasks with independent file/contract boundaries; avoid concurrent edits to the same stateful surface.
- ENTERPRISE work requires explicit human approval at architecture, security, and release gates.
- Do not claim completion until acceptance criteria and tests/verification have objective evidence.
- Preserve reversibility and a rollback path for production-affecting changes.
